{
  "esm": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "RecurrenceThirtyEightLags",
    "description": "The real lag scale, in ONE node. r[y] reads r at THIRTY-EIGHT distinct lags, each with its own weight P[a], under the banded filter a <= y-1, with a clamp max(r, 0) inside the fold.\n\nThis is the shape that made the format addition necessary rather than convenient. Three properties, each of which some cheaper design would have failed:\n\n1. THE LAG IS SYMBOL-VALUED. Thirty-eight lags are one `index(r, y - a)` with `a` contracted over [0, 38], not thirty-eight hand-written terms. A primitive admitting only a literal lag would have forced the generated, unfactored spelling.\n\n2. NO SCALAR ACCUMULATOR SUMMARISES THE HISTORY. The weights P[a] all differ, so there is no running value that could stand in for the previous thirty-eight answers -- which is exactly why the forward prefix scan of esm-spec 4.3.1, whose whole optimization is one carried accumulator, cannot express this and declines a body that reads its own output.\n\n3. THE CLAMP MAKES IT NON-LINEAR. max(r, 0) fires at 19 of the 40 cells (the residual goes negative at years 2, 3, 7, 9, 11, 13, ...), and it alters 38 of the 40 values relative to the same fold without it. So no linear closed form reproduces these numbers, and a Neumann-series expansion -- valid only where the clamp does not fire -- is wrong precisely here.\n\nThe expected values were computed by an INDEPENDENT reference: a direct ascending fold in Python, not by running this document. Zero tolerance.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "recurrence",
      "bounded-lag",
      "symbol-lag",
      "clamp",
      "non-linear",
      "independent-oracle"
    ]
  },
  "index_sets": {
    "years": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": 40
    }
  },
  "models": {
    "RecurrenceThirtyEightLags": {
      "tolerance": {
        "rel": 0.0,
        "abs": 0.0
      },
      "variables": {
        "r": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "years"
          ],
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Residual sequence: a non-recurrent term less the clamped, per-lag-weighted sum of its own thirty-eight previous values."
        }
      },
      "equations": [
        {
          "lhs": "r",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "aggregate",
            "args": [],
            "output_idx": [
              "y"
            ],
            "reduce": "+",
            "ranges": {
              "y": {
                "from": "years"
              },
              "a": [
                0,
                38
              ]
            },
            "filter": {
              "op": "<=",
              "args": [
                "a",
                {
                  "op": "-",
                  "args": [
                    "y",
                    1
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            "expr": {
              "op": "ifelse",
              "args": [
                {
                  "op": "==",
                  "args": [
                    "a",
                    0
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "op": "index",
                  "args": [
                    {
                      "op": "const",
                      "args": [],
                      "value": [
                        1.05,
                        1.1,
                        1.15,
                        1.2,
                        1.25,
                        1.3,
                        1.35,
                        1.4,
                        1.45,
                        1.5,
                        1.55,
                        1.6,
                        1.65,
                        1.7,
                        1.75,
                        1.8,
                        1.85,
                        1.9,
                        1.95,
                        2.0,
                        2.05,
                        2.1,
                        2.15,
                        2.2,
                        2.25,
                        2.3,
                        2.35,
                        2.4,
                        2.45,
                        2.5,
                        2.55,
                        2.6,
                        2.65,
                        2.7,
                        2.75,
                        2.8,
                        2.85,
                        2.9,
                        2.95,
                        3.0
                      ]
                    },
                    "y"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "op": "*",
                  "args": [
                    -1.0,
                    {
                      "op": "*",
                      "args": [
                        {
                          "op": "max",
                          "args": [
                            {
                              "op": "index",
                              "args": [
